ratic rating is warranted.", "watch": "A standout Fazio performance in the first debate or a late national shift against incumbent parties could narrow the margin, though the polling gap is large.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["Incumbent Ned Lamont (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Connecticut's governor's race pits incumbent Democrat Ned Lamont, seeking a third term, against state Senator Ryan Fazio. Lamont enters the final weeks with a clear advantage in a state that leans Democratic by eight points. Polling from Quinnipiac, Emerson, the University of New Hampshire and Wesleyan/YouGov shows Lamont ahead by thirteen to twenty-three points, with the broad average near eighteen. Even the most favorable poll for Fazio, from a Republican-leaning firm, showed a seven-point Lamont lead.\n\nEvery major race rating places the contest in the Solid or Safe Democratic column, and prediction markets price Lamont's chances at roughly ninety-six to ninety-seven percent. Voter dissatisfaction with the national economy and the Trump administration has weighed on Fazio's campaign. The first debate gives Fazio a chance to alter the race's trajectory, but the evidence points to a comfortable Lamont reelection.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.994, "margin": 15.28}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9913, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9896, "margin": 13.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9893, "margin": 14.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9879, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9857, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9868, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9861, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9879, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9889, "margin": 14.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.989, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9875, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9908, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem":